ajc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manirajc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manirajc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manirajc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Is your feature request related to a specific problem?\n\nFeature Description\nAdd a explicit `/compact` command and a visible context fullness percentage bar to the Antigravity UI and CLI interface, mirroring the context lifecycle engineering found in Codex and Claude Code. \nProblem Statement\nIn Antigravity 2.11.0, long-running agent trajectories accumulate huge payloads of tool call schemas, background command outputs, and localized database maps. When the sequence becomes bloated, the local UI client aggressively clings to the active Trajectory ID, resubmitting the entire overhead until it hits upstream gateway validation bugs (throwing `HTTP 400 Bad Request / INVALID_ARGUMENT` loops even on basic text inputs). \n\nCurrently, users must manually discard their broken chat histories and orchestrate a manual context handoff to a fresh chat window to escape the block.\n\n### Describe the solution you'd like\n\n1. **CLI Macro Command**: Expose a manual `/compact` or `/summarize` command parameter to prune tool execution histories while retaining active context, project schemas, and variable state.\n2. **Visual Fullness Gauge**: Implement a status pill in the UI input box showing context health (e.g., `Compact this chat's context (47% full)`).\n3. **Proactive Auto-Compaction**: Add a configurable background trigger threshold (e.g., `preemptive_compaction_threshold: 0.80`) that safely compresses historical model turns before the underlying serialization limits crash the gateway payload.\n\n### Describe alternatives you've considered\n\n/compact in CODEX\n\n### Additional context\n\nThis issue directly prevents the frustrating locked-trajectory loops that require deleting local application data or switching workspace folders just to revive an active project session","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-antigravity/antigravity-cli/issues/919/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-antigravity/antigravity-cli/issues/919/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}